1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,871
From one ticket to a project with many PRs:
agents do the work, you keep the decisions and approvals.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:19,629
A Claude Code plugin with four kinds of parts:
41 skills, 4 agent definitions, 10 hooks, and commands

3
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:30,851
Skills fire when their situation shows up, or by name.
Hooks step in before and after an action, and can stop it.

4
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:40,129
Human in the loop: approve each step.
Human on the loop: agents run, you step in on exceptions.

5
00:00:40,534 --> 00:00:52,941
Owner → one orchestrator → one lead per project
→ cards (one ticket each, own worktree)

6
00:00:53,367 --> 00:01:05,510
The orchestrator writes no PR: it routes and judges.
One PR → a /goal card. Several related PRs → a lead.

7
00:01:05,934 --> 00:01:19,689
Built on Orca: a terminal per worktree, a Run for the goal, mail.
The lead keeps one background wait and wakes on news.

8
00:01:20,101 --> 00:01:30,061
Plan → build (own worktree) → test → review by a non-author
→ PR → CI

9
00:01:30,468 --> 00:01:43,913
The worker lands its own PR with orch land, only when every check passes,
then watches main CI and reports worker_done with evidence.

10
00:01:44,335 --> 00:01:55,943
Ledger → program directory · machine state → local state
tickets → tracker · reasoning → notes · PRs and CI → GitHub

11
00:01:56,368 --> 00:02:06,036
dispatch-card opens a card, deliver-ticket carries a ticket to done,
and orchestrate runs the whole program.

12
00:02:06,468 --> 00:02:18,086
record-progress records, end-session closes, brief reports,
watch-prs gathers reviews, reap-resources cleans up.

13
00:02:18,502 --> 00:02:29,764
The dashboard is a local page; it spends no tokens.
Board: progress, main CI, in flight vs cap, land order.

14
00:02:30,169 --> 00:02:36,822
Stages: one row per item — PR, merged, dev check, prod check.

15
00:02:37,236 --> 00:02:43,796
To-do: dated and conditional to-dos, and the held queue.
Overdue items turn red.

16
00:02:44,203 --> 00:02:52,584
Inbox: everything waiting on you, by type.
Answer a decision with a button; it goes back to the lead.

17
00:02:53,003 --> 00:02:59,444
PR stats: PRs you and your agents opened, by month and source.
Collected every 6 hours.

18
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:08,384
A day: you ask → the request is logged
→ the orchestrator starts a lead

19
00:03:08,803 --> 00:03:19,078
The lead pilots one card, then adds one per green landing.
Each card opens a PR and gets an independent review.

20
00:03:19,503 --> 00:03:27,302
Land → release and check → one brief to the owner:
done, in progress, decisions needed

21
00:03:27,703 --> 00:03:39,740
Around the clock: wait in the background, watch-cards finds stuck cards,
the janitor cleans up every 3 hours.

22
00:03:40,170 --> 00:03:47,477
Machine load is measured every 3 minutes.
At the danger level, heavy starts are refused and queued.

23
00:03:47,903 --> 00:04:02,291
The auto-mode classifier judges every act; a refused act is never retried.
Hooks and a separate guard plugin watch too.

24
00:04:02,703 --> 00:04:14,769
Approvals, permission prompts, logins, irreversible acts: human only.
Collected in one inbox and sent to you in one batch.

25
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:23,971
Agents carry the work, state stays in the ledger and dashboard,
and you keep the decisions and approvals.

